* Detection: Portfolio IOC sweep — hunt every indicator from this portfolio at once
* Author:    Beltus Bejanga
* Related:   IP-Investigation-001, Malware-Analysis-001, Phishing-Email-Analysis-001
* Data:      Firewall / proxy / DNS / EDR logs. Adjust index + field names to your env.
* Idea:      One scheduled search that lights up if ANY known-bad indicator appears
*            anywhere in the environment.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Network indicators — attacker + C2 IPs, phishing domain
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
index=* (
      src_ip IN ("157.66.224.37","82.157.13.47")
   OR dest_ip IN ("157.66.224.37","82.157.13.47")
   OR query="*oluwaburnazip--renusharawat.replit.app*"
   OR url="*oluwaburnazip--renusharawat.replit.app*"
)
| eval ioc=coalesce(dest_ip,src_ip,query,url)
| eval ioc_type=case(
      ioc=="157.66.224.37","Brute-force source (IP-Investigation-001)",
      ioc=="82.157.13.47","Malware C2 (Malware-Analysis-001)",
      like(ioc,"%replit.app%"),"Phishing site (Phishing-Email-Analysis-001)")
| stats count min(_time) as first max(_time) as last
        values(host) as hosts values(user) as users by ioc ioc_type
| eval first=strftime(first,"%F %T"), last=strftime(last,"%F %T")
| sort - count

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 File hash indicator — whack.sh dropper (needs EDR / Sysmon-for-Linux hashes)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 index=* (
       file_hash="36dabc40fa8983ce900a90b8156d2c754875fe1b5413a997843c4a0ef3908220"
    OR sha256="36dabc40fa8983ce900a90b8156d2c754875fe1b5413a997843c4a0ef3908220"
 )
 | stats count values(host) as hosts values(process) as processes by file_hash
 | eval verdict="whack.sh dropper present — ISOLATE host, preserve memory"

---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 Host behaviour — whack.sh masquerades as a kernel worker thread
 (a REAL [kworker/...] is a kernel thread with no executable image on disk;
  a userland process using that name is the giveaway)
---------------------------------------------------------------------------
 index=* sourcetype=sysmon_linux EventID=1 process_name="[kworker/*"
 | stats count values(parent_process) as parents values(process_path) as paths by host process_name
 | eval verdict="Process masquerading as kernel worker — investigate immediately"
